  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reconciled all five patients' outpatient medication lists against their St. Brigid discharge documents under RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a progress note for each. New results and addenda came in while I was working, and three of them changed decisions I had already made; I corrected those.\n\n**Walter Kim (pt-0005)**\n- **Furosemide:** now 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). The signed addendum overrides the summary's 40 mg once daily.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped, as the discharge summary says.\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. Pantoprazole was only a hospital formulary swap, so I didn't order it.\n- **Lisinopril:** I first kept it on hold because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat test today showed potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21 (the discharge rule was to resume once creatinine is below 1.5), so I resumed it (mr-00072).\n- **Open task:** my earlier task to recheck potassium (task-t0003) is no longer needed. The system wouldn't let me close it, so please close it.\n- **Draft addendum:** an unsigned draft proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily came in. Only signed addenda count, so I didn't act on it.\n- Metoprolol, atorvastatin and aspirin are unchanged.\n\n**Terence Stark (pt-0004)**\n- **Carvedilol:** I raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary (\"Coreg\"). A signed addendum then arrived reversing the increase (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing). I changed the order back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0017).\n- **Flagged — atorvastatin:** last filled 03/04/2026, so fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission (the cutoff is 80%). I left the order as is and messaged you (comm-t0006).\n- **Flagged — glipizide 5 mg:** an outside doctor (Dr. Desai) prescribes it, filled monthly, with no clinic order. The discharge summary doesn't mention it. I made no change and messaged you (comm-t0007); taking it with insulin 70/30 risks low blood sugar.\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 are unchanged.\n\n**Earnest Roberts (pt-0044)**\n- **Lisinopril:** I resumed it (creatinine 1.08, potassium 4.6 on 10/22). A new potassium of 5.5 then arrived from 10/23, so I put it back on hold (mr-00373). I created a task for you to recheck potassium, due 10/26 (task-t0018).\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin are unchanged.\n\n**Gerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)**\n- **Lisinopril:** resumed (mr-69003). Creatinine was 1.12 and potassium 4.4 on 10/21.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin are unchanged.\n- The discharge plan also asked for a potassium 3 days after discharge. It isn't in the chart yet.\n\n**Lorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)**\n- **Metformin:** still on hold (mr-67001). The only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, which doesn't meet the \"post-discharge labs\" condition. I created a task for you, due 10/24, to resume it if creatinine is below 1.5 on that day's blood test (task-t0013).\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin are unchanged.\n\n**Needs you**\n- Terence: atorvastatin adherence and the outside glipizide.\n- Earnest: lisinopril after the repeat potassium.\n- Lorraine: metformin after the 10/24 blood test.\n- Walter: close the outdated potassium task (task-t0003).\n\nI closed the four new inbox items for these patients, each linked to the action taken. Your other inbox items are for other patients and I left them alone.",
